  "agent": {
    "note": "candidate-001 — first cut of @m0saic/alpine/line-chart/v1. Standalone Alpine brand flavor (white card, soft translucent area wash, rounded primary line, point markers w/ white halo, left value-tick rail, bottom month labels, hairline gridlines). Every mark is a tight cell-local inline-mask placed full-canvas via placeRects (the donut's seam-free recipe); reuses pure path MATH from charts/line-chart/v1/geometry (curve flatten, stroke ribbon, area polygon). Curve options: smooth (default) / linear / stepped. INTRO = a left→right CURTAIN WIPE: the whole chart is built static (crisp), then one card-colored rectangle slides off to the right to reveal it. (I first tried a per-sliver line draw-on, but the many overlapping sliver masks each spill to their own overlay layer, and past ~25 nested overlay layers this engine drops inline-masks — circle markers collapsed to squares, labels rasterized to tofu. The curtain adds exactly ONE overlay layer over the proven-clean static chart: no depth blow-up, clean premium wipe.) Dual props: Animate / Intro length / Area fill / Point markers / Gridlines sliders+checkboxes drive the canonical anim/area/points/grid groups. Verified clean at end + mid frames, smooth/linear/stepped, light/dark, and 12 edge cases (single point, 2pt, flat, negatives, 20 points, no-area/grid/points/labels).",
    "question": "First look at the Alpine line chart. Scrub the timeline — the curtain wipe reveals the chart left→right. Does the look land (area softness, line weight, marker halo, gridline/label balance, type scale), and does the wipe feel good? This is candidate-001; I'll iterate the look one nudge at a time. (Open question if you have a preference: the x-axis month labels currently stay visible during the wipe — the axis frame is present while the content wipes in. I can also make them wipe in with the curtain.)"
  }
